From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
Date: 2026-09-01
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sm6125: laurel: fix reserved-memory node name and ramoops binding

Downstream-only fix for the frozen 6.1 fork at
77de535b8dbd8f483b5802c8937cb714bab5b485.

The board DTS defined the reserved memory node as `reserved_memory`
(underscore). The kernel (drivers/of/of_reserved_mem.c) only recognizes
/reserved-memory (hyphen) as the reserved-memory binding container.
Nodes declared under /reserved_memory are never processed by
of_reserved_mem, so ramoops/pstore, debug_mem, last_log_mem and
cmdline_mem were silently ignored at runtime (validated: /proc/iomem and
/proc/device-tree/reserved-memory expose the sm6125.dtsi regions but not
these board regions, and /sys/fs/pstore stays empty even though a ramoops
node exists in the built DTB).

Fix:
- rename node `reserved_memory` -> `reserved-memory` so the kernel
  processes the board reserved regions as direct children of the
  standard /reserved-memory container;
- fix the ramoops child: the binding
  (Documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/ramoops.yaml) has no
  `msg-size` property; the correct property is `pmsg-size` with a single
  cell.  Update the node accordingly.

While here, align the node unit-address with the actual reg base
(cosmetic; dtc warns when the node name unit address does not match reg).

Signed-off-by: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125-xiaomi-laurel_sprout.dts | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125-xiaomi-laurel_sprout.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125-xiaomi-laurel_sprout.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125-xiaomi-laurel_sprout.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125-xiaomi-laurel_sprout.dts
@@ -39,6 +39,6 @@
 		id-gpio = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	};
 
-	reserved_memory {
+	reserved-memory {
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
@@ -52,13 +52,13 @@
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		pstore_mem: ramoops@ffc00000 {
+		pstore_mem: ramoops@ffc40000 {
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0x0 0xffc40000 0x0 0xc0000>;
 			record-size = <0x1000>;
 			console-size = <0x40000>;
-			msg-size = <0x20000 0x20000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
 		};
 
-		cmdline_mem: memory@ffd00000 {
+		cmdline_mem: memory@ffd40000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0xffd40000 0x0 0x1000>;
-- 
